{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/nx/schemas/nx-schema.json",
  "installation": {
    "version": "22.7.0"
  },
  /* So a local `nx affected` compares against the same branch CI does. Without
     it Nx infers a base, and the inference differs between a fresh clone and a
     long-lived checkout — the two disagree silently, in the direction of
     selecting too little. */
  "defaultBase": "main",
  "namedInputs": {
    /* Spelled out because Nx's implicit `default` is the project's own files
       ALONE — it does not include `sharedGlobals`. Only the nx.json that `nx
       init` generates lists both, and this workspace was never generated by
       it. Declaring `sharedGlobals` without this line parses, validates, shows
       up in `readNxJson()`, and hashes nothing: measured, a brand-doc edit
       still left `nx run-many -t build` at 7/7 cache hits. See
       node_modules/nx/dist/src/hasher/task-hasher.js:120.
       (Comments here are block comments and Nx parses this file as JSONC, so
       no comment may contain a glob ending in a star-slash — it closes the
       comment and Nx dies with `InvalidSymbol`.) */
    "default": ["{projectRoot}/**/*", "sharedGlobals"],
    /* `design-system-docs/` belongs to no project and is read by five of them:
       apps/docs stages it into public/brand and reads it again at request time
       (src/lib/brand.ts, src/lib/ai-corpus.ts); ai-patterns walks it to build
       brand-manifest.json and asserts over it in five test files; tokens tests
       parse its stylesheets; storybook's MarketingPattern stories import from
       it. None of that is an import edge Nx can see.
       Measured before this line existed: appending a comment to
       design-system-docs/guidelines/brand-voice.html left `nx run-many -t
       build` at 7/7 cache hits, so a brand-docs-only PR replayed a stale
       brand-manifest.json — and with `.nx/cache` now restored across CI runs
       (a987bf3), stale across runs too.
       `sharedGlobals` rather than a per-target input on the five, deliberately:
       the failure is silent and the list only grows. Everything cacheable is
       invalidated by a brand edit, which is the correct blast radius — #93
       measured that this directory feeds the docs sidebar on every page.
       README.md is excluded because ai-patterns' build WRITES it (the managed
       index table is generated from the manifest). In the input set it would
       make its own build's hash oscillate: build, README changes, next hash
       misses, rebuild. It is derived, not source.
       The trailing double-star is load-bearing and the obvious spelling is
       wrong. A fileset of `design-system-docs/` plus double-star-slash-star
       matched nothing here and hashed nothing — same silent 7/7 as declaring
       no input at all. Verified both ways against the same probe: brand-doc
       edit rebuilds, README-only edit stays 4/4 cached. */
    "sharedGlobals": [
      "{workspaceRoot}/design-system-docs/**",
      "!{workspaceRoot}/design-system-docs/README.md"
    ]
  },
  "targetDefaults": {
    "build": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "outputs": ["{projectRoot}/dist"],
      "cache": true
    },
    /* Neither writes anything: every `test` is `vitest run` with no coverage
       reporter configured, or an `echo` placeholder, and every `lint` is
       `eslint .` or an `echo`. No `outputs` to declare, so a replay restores
       nothing and only the terminal output comes back — which is the whole
       artifact of these two targets.
       The `echo 'No tests configured'` placeholders in create-elirobinson-
       design-system and storybook cache like anything else. They are not
       coverage and must not be counted as any. */
    "test": {
      "cache": true
    },
    "lint": {
      "cache": true
    }
  },
  "analytics": true
}
